    <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
    <h1>Terms of service</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated <span class="ph">[go-live date]</span> · <a href="/da/vilkaar" hreflang="da">Dansk version</a></p>
    <p class="draft"><b>Draft for legal review.</b> Written for business customers only. Placeholders are highlighted.</p>

    <section class="short" aria-labelledby="short-h">
      <h2 id="short-h">The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Kupro is for businesses. You own your data; we host it in the EU and give it back when you leave.</li>
        <li>You are responsible for what your people and your agents do with their access.</li>
        <li>The meeting agent suggests changes. Tell people in the meeting it is listening.</li>
        <li>Pay per seat, monthly or yearly, in advance. Cancel any time; it ends with the period you paid for. No refunds for part periods.</li>
        <li>Danish law, Copenhagen courts.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <h2 id="t1">1. Agreement</h2>
    <p>These terms are an agreement between Pilgaard Development, CVR 41249269 ("we") and the company or
      organisation that creates or pays for a Kupro workspace ("you"). The person who accepts them confirms they may bind that
      organisation. Kupro is offered to businesses only; consumer protection rules for private buyers don't apply.</p>
    <p>Our <a href="/dpa">data processing agreement</a> is part of these terms. Our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> explains how we handle
      the personal data we control.</p>

    <h2 id="t2">2. Accounts and workspaces</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A <b>workspace</b> belongs to you. Its owners invite members and guests, set roles and can delete it.</li>
      <li>Each person needs their own account. Keep sign-in details private and turn on two-factor authentication where we offer it.</li>
      <li>Tell us at <a href="mailto:contact@kupro.app">contact@kupro.app</a> straight away if you think an account or token has been misused.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="t3">3. Agents and tokens</h2>
    <p>You can let software agents use Kupro through the API, the CLI or MCP with tokens you create. An agent acts with the
      permissions of the person or workspace that created its token. You are responsible for what your agents do, the same as for
      your members. Revoke a token to stop an agent at once. We may rate-limit or pause a token that harms the service for others,
      and we tell you when we do.</p>

    <h2 id="t4">4. Meeting agent</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The meeting agent listens only during a session someone in your workspace starts. It suggests issue changes; in suggest mode
        nothing changes until a person approves it.</li>
      <li>If an admin turns on full auto, changes are applied without approval and can be undone. You decide which kinds of change are allowed.</li>
      <li><b>You must tell everyone in a meeting that it is being processed</b>, and get consent where the law where you are requires it.
        Don't use it in meetings where recording would be unlawful or where participants have objected.</li>
      <li>Transcription and suggestions can be wrong, especially with names, accents and mixed languages. Check what you approve.</li>
      <li>Audio is not stored. Transcripts are deleted when the meeting ends, unless an owner sets a retention period. Details are in the <a href="/privacy#meetings">privacy policy</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="t5">5. Your data</h2>
    <p>Everything you and your agents put into a workspace is yours. You give us the right to host, copy, process and show it only
      as needed to run Kupro for you. We don't use it for anything else, and we don't use it to train AI models.</p>
    <p>Owners can export a workspace at any time as a ZIP file with JSON, CSV and the attached files, from Settings in the app, the API or the CLI. An export can be downloaded for 7 days.</p>

    <h2 id="t6">6. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Don't use Kupro to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>break the law, or store content you have no right to store;</li>
      <li>upload malware, or try to reach other customers' data or our systems beyond your access;</li>
      <li>overload the service on purpose, or get around rate limits, seat counts or plan limits;</li>
      <li>resell the hosted service without a written agreement with us.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Security research is welcome: report what you find to <a href="mailto:contact@kupro.app">contact@kupro.app</a> and give us reasonable time to fix it before you publish. We may suspend access that puts the service or other
      customers at risk. Where we can, we warn you first and give you time to fix it.</p>

    <h2 id="t7">7. Plans and payment</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Prices are on our pricing page and are in euro (EUR) or Danish kroner (DKK), whichever you choose when you subscribe, excluding VAT. We add VAT where it applies.</li>
      <li>Paid plans are billed per seat. A seat is an active member with the Owner or Member role, whether or not they use the
        service. Guests and agents don't need a seat, within the limits on the pricing page. We show you which seats have not
        been used for 30 days and remind you before a yearly renewal, so you can remove them.</li>
      <li>You pay in advance for each month or year. Adding seats mid-period is charged pro rata; removing seats takes effect at the next renewal.</li>
      <li>Subscriptions renew automatically until cancelled. You can cancel in the app; it ends at the close of the period you paid for.
        We don't refund part periods.</li>
      <li>Custom plans follow the agreement we make with you; where it differs from these terms, the agreement applies.</li>
      <li>Payments are handled by Alunta and our card acquirer <span class="ph">[OnPay or QuickPay, chosen before billing starts]</span>. If a payment fails we email you; after
        14 days unpaid we may make the workspace read-only until it is paid.</li>
      <li>We announce price changes at least 60 days ahead. They apply from your next renewal after that.</li>
      <li>A new workspace starts with a free 30-day trial of the full service, with the limits on the pricing page. When it ends, the workspace is read-only until you subscribe, and is deleted 30 days later if you don't. You can export it the whole time.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="t8">8. Availability and changes to the service</h2>
    <p>We aim to keep Kupro fast and available and tell workspace owners by email about incidents that affect them. We don't promise a
      specific uptime on standard plans. We announce planned maintenance that may interrupt the service at least 48 hours ahead.</p>
    <p>Kupro changes as we build it. We won't remove a core feature you rely on (issues, sprints, delivery plan, export, the API)
      without 90 days' notice.</p>

    <h2 id="t9">9. Ending</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You can stop at any time by cancelling and deleting your workspace.</li>
      <li>We can end the agreement with 90 days' notice, or at once if you seriously breach these terms and don't fix it within 14 days of our notice.</li>
      <li>After a subscription ends, the workspace stays read-only and exportable for 30 days. Then we delete it. Backups roll off within
        35 days after that.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="t10">10. Open source</h2>
    <p>Kupro's source code is published under the GNU Affero General Public License v3. These terms cover our hosted service, not
      the code. You can run the code yourself under the AGPL; if you do, these terms don't apply to that installation.
      The Kupro name and logo are ours; don't use them for your own hosted service without permission.</p>

    <h2 id="t11">11. Liability</h2>
    <p>Each party's total liability under this agreement is limited to the fees you paid us in the 12 months before the claim.
      Neither party is liable for indirect loss, such as lost profit, lost revenue or lost goodwill. These limits don't apply to
      breaches of confidentiality, your payment obligations, or damage caused by gross negligence or intent.</p>
    <p>During the trial, Kupro is free and provided as is. We are not liable for any loss from using it, except where the law doesn't allow liability to be excluded, such as for intent or gross negligence.</p>
    <p>Neither party is responsible for delays caused by events outside its reasonable control, such as major internet or power
      failures, war, or actions by authorities.</p>

    <h2 id="t12">12. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>We email workspace owners at least 30 days before changes that affect you take effect. If you don't agree, you can cancel before
      then and we refund any prepaid fees for the remaining period. Small corrections and clarifications take effect when published.</p>

    <h2 id="t13">13. Law and disputes</h2>
    <p>Danish law governs this agreement, excluding its conflict-of-laws rules. We'll try to settle disagreements by talking first. If
      that fails, disputes go to the Copenhagen City Court (Københavns Byret) as the first instance.</p>
    <p>Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:contact@kupro.app">contact@kupro.app</a>.</p>
